<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>(a) A plot in Kajiado was valued at Ksh <m>{460\,000}</m> and one year later at Ksh <m>{506\,000}</m>. Find the rate of appreciation, as a percentage.</p><p><fillin characters="5" name="ans1"/> %  </p><p>(b) A house in Ruiru rose in value from Ksh <m>{1\,200\,000}</m> to Ksh <m>{1\,452\,000}</m> in <m>2</m> years, appreciating at the same rate each year. Find the yearly rate of appreciation.</p><p><fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/> %  </p><p>Give each answer exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The increase is <m>{506\,000} - {460\,000} = {46\,000}</m>. As a percentage of the starting value:</p><p><me>\frac{{46\,000}}{{460\,000}} \times 100 = {10}\%.</me></p><p>(b) Over two years the value is multiplied by <m>\left(1 + \frac{r}{100}\right)^2</m>, so</p><p><me>\left(1 + \frac{r}{100}\right)^2 = \frac{{1\,452\,000}}{{1\,200\,000}} = {1.21}, \qquad 1 + \frac{r}{100} = \sqrt{ {1.21} } = {1.1}.</me></p><p>The yearly rate is <m>{10}\%</m>. Halving the total rise of <m>{21}\%</m> gives <m>{10.5}\%</m>, which is too big: each year's rise is on a bigger value.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>10</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>10</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>